sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-08> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Lateral spine of Schistosoma eggs is moulded in the ootype, not a species mark" ;
    dct:description "Following Looss, the lateral spine of some Schistosoma eggs is moulded mechanically in a funnel-shaped part of the uterus, so lateral- and terminal-spined eggs are mechanical variants of one thing and do not show the existence of a separate species, S. mansoni." ;
    delphi:context "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XV, “On the Shapes of Eggs, and of Certain Other Hollow Structures”; topic “Eggs of Schistosoma”. Scope: eggs of Schistosoma haematobium and S. mansoni" ;
    dct:type "mechanism" .
}

